/-!
# The ball environment of the nesting chain of the Dommaschk tori C and A

The nesting chain extends the low-resolution admissibility chain of torus A
(`Design/DommaschkKamAAdmEnv`, variables `0, …, 194`, layout `32 × 32`, scale `2^{−64}`, oracle
angle `ψₒ = 2φ`) by 27 variables with unit strip weights (`ρ = 0`): the surrogate of torus C
embedded in the layout (`embC`, no new data) without its `θ`-average (`X_C`, `Y_C`), the surrogate
of torus A minus the same average (`X_A`, `Y_A`), `cos θ`, `sin θ`, the gauge coefficients, the
radial functions, the gauge values, the approximate inverse square roots and their squares. The
lists are the Adm lists followed by the new entries (`xN_lt`, `BN_lt`, `EN_lt`). Generated by
`scripts/dommaschk_kam/emit_nest.py`.
-/

@[expose] public section
noncomputable section

namespace PlasmaLean.Design.DommaschkKamA

